---
layout: base.njk
permalink: /consulting/
title: Consulting
description: Architecture and engineering consulting from JD Carlston, hourly, by scope or by the block, from a two-hour consultation to a legacy migration plan.
---
<section class="art-top">
  {% set faint = true %}{% include "hero-art.njk" %}
<div class="section wrap consult-hero">
  <div class="sechead">
    <h1 class="h1--page">Consulting</h1>
  </div>
  <p class="lede consult-lede">When the system starts slowing your people down, it's time for another set of eyes.</p>
  <p class="intro">Maybe it sounds like this:</p>
  <ul class="pains">
    <li>A change that used to take two days now takes two weeks, and nobody can tell you why.</li>
    <li>You’ve had the same architecture debate three times, and nobody can find why you decided it the first time.</li>
    <li>Everyone’s busy, everyone’s blocked, and it takes days to find out who owns the thing that broke.</li>
    <li>The migration is in year two, both systems are still live, and your best engineers are starting to avoid it.</li>
    <li>You acquired a company and inherited two auth systems, two pipelines and two definitions of done.</li>
    <li>Your CFO keeps asking what the AI tools are buying you, and you don’t have clean numbers.</li>
  </ul>
  <p class="intro">I’ve sat in those rooms as a VP, as a Senior Director, as an architect, and as an engineer. I come in, find the real constraint, and work alongside your people. Hourly, by the project or by the block of time, whatever fits your needs.</p>
  <div class="actions">
    <a class="btn btn--solid" href="#inquire">Send an inquiry</a>
    <a class="btn btn--line" href="{{ consulting.calendly }}">Book a free consult</a>
  </div>
</div>
</section>

<section class="section-band">
  <div class="section wrap">
    <ol class="offers">
      {% for o in consulting.offers %}
      <li class="offer" id="{{ o.id }}">
        <div class="offer__head">
          <p class="mono teal small">{{ loop.index }} · {{ o.step }}</p>
          <h2>{{ o.name }}</h2>
          <p class="mono muted small">{{ o.format }}</p>
        </div>
        <div class="offer__body">
          <p>{{ o.summary }}</p>
          <p class="mono teal small">you get</p>
          <ul>
            {% for d in o.deliverables %}<li>{{ d }}</li>{% endfor %}
          </ul>
          <p class="muted"><strong>Good for:</strong> {{ o.goodFor }}</p>
          <a class="offer__ask" href="?service={{ o.id }}#inquire">Ask about {{ o.name }} →</a>
        </div>
      </li>
      {% endfor %}
    </ol>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section-band" id="inquire">
  <div class="section wrap split">
    <div class="split__main">
      <div class="sechead">
        <h2>Tell me about your problem</h2>
      </div>
      <p class="intro">Please let me know what you’re up against. You’ll get my calendar link to book a preliminary consultation. I read every inquiry and reply personally within two business days.</p>
      <form class="form" name="consulting" method="POST" action="/consulting/thanks/" data-netlify="true" netlify-honeypot="company_url">
        <input type="hidden" name="form-name" value="consulting">
        <p class="hp"><label>Leave this empty <input name="company_url" tabindex="-1" autocomplete="off"></label></p>
        <div class="form__row">
          <div class="field">
            <label for="f-name">Name</label>
            <input id="f-name" name="name" type="text" autocomplete="name" required>
          </div>
          <div class="field">
            <label for="f-email">Email</label>
            <input id="f-email" name="email" type="email" autocomplete="email" required>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="form__row">
          <div class="field">
            <label for="f-org">Organization</label>
            <input id="f-org" name="organization" type="text" autocomplete="organization">
          </div>
          <div class="field">
            <label for="f-service">What you're interested in</label>
            <select id="f-service" name="service">
              <option value="not-sure">Not sure yet</option>
              {% for o in consulting.offers %}<option value="{{ o.id }}">{{ o.name }}</option>{% endfor %}
            </select>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="field">
          <label for="f-message">What's going on?</label>
          <textarea id="f-message" name="message" rows="6" required></textarea>
        </div>
        <div class="form__row">
          <div class="field">
            <label for="f-phone">Mobile number <span class="optional">(optional)</span></label>
            <input id="f-phone" name="phone" type="tel" autocomplete="tel" inputmode="tel">
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="checks">
          <label class="check"><input type="checkbox" name="text_ok" value="yes"> It's OK to text me about this inquiry.</label>
          <label class="check"><input type="checkbox" name="updates" value="yes"> Also send me occasional updates and new writing. Unsubscribe anytime.</label>
        </div>
        <button class="btn btn--solid" type="submit">Send inquiry</button>
      </form>
    </div>
    <aside class="split__side">
      <p class="mono teal small">rather talk first?</p>
      <a class="linkcard" href="{{ consulting.calendly }}">
        <span class="mono teal small">Free preliminary consult →</span>
        <span class="linkcard__title">Book a time on my calendar</span>
      </a>
      <p class="muted small-print">Engagements are contracted through Red Thread Labs LLC.</p>
    </aside>
  </div>
</section>

<script>
  // Preselect the service when someone arrives from an "Ask about" link.
  (function () {
    var s = new URLSearchParams(location.search).get("service");
    var sel = document.getElementById("f-service");
    if (s && sel && sel.querySelector('option[value="' + s.replace(/[^a-z-]/g, "") + '"]')) sel.value = s;
  })();

  // On submit, send the inquiry to Netlify, then go straight to Calendly
  // with name and email filled in. Without JavaScript, the form posts
  // normally and the thanks page forwards to Calendly instead.
  (function () {
    var form = document.querySelector('form[name="consulting"]');
    if (!form || !window.fetch) return;
    var calendly = "{{ consulting.calendly }}";
    form.addEventListener("submit", function (e) {
      e.preventDefault();
      var data = new FormData(form);
      var btn = form.querySelector('button[type="submit"], .btn');
      if (btn) btn.disabled = true;
      fetch("/", {
        method: "POST",
        headers: { "Content-Type": "application/x-www-form-urlencoded" },
        body: new URLSearchParams(data).toString()
      }).then(function (r) {
        if (!r.ok) throw new Error(r.status);
        var q = new URLSearchParams({ name: data.get("name") || "", email: data.get("email") || "" });
        location.href = calendly + "?" + q.toString();
      }).catch(function () {
        if (btn) btn.disabled = false;
        form.submit();
      });
    });
  })();
</script>
